- Who makes no sense at all, ever.


00:12:57.629 --> 00:12:59.392
Why don't you have another drink, Mom.


00:13:00.933 --> 00:13:03.128
Katie, napkin me.


00:13:03.302 --> 00:13:05.793
I have got to impress Guy Morgan...


00:13:06.205 --> 00:13:09.436
...so I can stop pretending to care
about this insufferable school...


00:13:09.608 --> 00:13:13.374
...and we can all move to Hollywood where
no one pretends to care about anything.


00:13:13.545 --> 00:13:17.174
Mom, I think that you're forgetting
about the most important thing. Me.


00:13:18.116 --> 00:13:20.516
Guy will give me a deal
as soon as he hears me sing.


00:13:20.686 --> 00:13:23.280
- I doubt that.
- No, I've been practicing really hard.


00:13:23.455 --> 00:13:26.322
My voice teacher says
I've transcended to a whole new level.


00:13:26.492 --> 00:13:27.516
Yeah, I doubt it.


00:13:27.693 --> 00:13:30.253
When my first single drops,
I'll buy you that mansion...


00:13:30.429 --> 00:13:32.363
...in the Hollywood Hills...


00:13:32.531 --> 00:13:35.557
...and you can finally afford
to have your legs lengthened.


00:13:35.734 --> 00:13:37.759
- Oh, ba...
- Ms. Gail.


00:13:37.936 --> 00:13:39.904
- Miss Bev has clarity.
Katie.


00:13:40.072 --> 00:13:41.096
- You see...
- Look.


00:13:41.273 --> 00:13:45.141
- The lowly peasant tills the soil
for 40 years without any rain.


00:13:45.310 --> 00:13:48.711
But the unemployed salesman
who has recently discovered hydroponics...


00:13:48.881 --> 00:13:51.975
...all of a sudden gets disgusted by the...
- And see? No sense.


00:13:52.150 --> 00:13:54.448
- That didn't make any sense.
- Let me finish. You...


00:13:54.620 --> 00:13:56.554
Oh, I doubt it. You have me pray all day.


00:13:56.722 --> 00:13:58.952
- I don't feel nothing.
- You don't have a soul.


00:13:59.124 --> 00:14:02.321
No, you don't have soul.
- I have a many souls. I'll give you one.


00:14:02.494 --> 00:14:06.760
- Where's your third eye? Turn that thing on.
- I have a fourth eye too. You wanna see it?


00:14:06.932 --> 00:14:08.900
- What?
- Shh.


00:14:09.401 --> 00:14:12.928
I wanna be 6'4". Wow me, Bev.


00:14:15.474 --> 00:14:20.912
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do</i>


00:14:21.079 --> 00:14:23.639
Just stop. Stop the wowing, okay?


00:14:23.815 --> 00:14:25.908
What's wrong?
- Somehow you've gotten worse.


00:14:26.084 --> 00:14:27.813
I don't know how that was possible...


00:14:27.986 --> 00:14:30.614
...but there isn't enough Auto-Tune
that's gonna fix you.


00:14:30.789 --> 00:14:34.122
- Well, Katie's bad playing threw me off.
- I don't think it was that.


00:14:34.293 --> 00:14:35.920
Again.


00:14:36.094 --> 00:14:37.652
Really? Okay.


00:14:37.829 --> 00:14:43.461
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do</i>


00:14:43.635 --> 00:14:44.761
Ouch.


00:14:44.937 --> 00:14:47.997
I could belch the song better.


00:14:49.608 --> 00:14:51.769
Have you been drinking
the floor wax again?


00:14:51.944 --> 00:14:53.411
Anything to forget I live here.


00:14:53.579 --> 00:14:56.480
Ugh. My head is buzzing
like a skeeter on a septic tank.


00:14:56.648 --> 00:15:00.550
- Ravi, meditate me.
Good luck, buddy.


00:15:00.919 --> 00:15:04.582
Well, it doesn't matter,
because I have my own plan.


00:15:08.794 --> 00:15:11.160
Does it make me a bad person
that I kind of enjoyed that?


00:15:11.330 --> 00:15:13.059
No.


00:15:13.231 --> 00:15:15.529
Hmm. Nice work.


00:15:27.713 --> 00:15:31.012
- Guess who's on his way over.
- Not now, Victor, I'm busy.


00:15:31.183 --> 00:15:33.651
Guess or prepare to get creamed.


00:15:44.129 --> 00:15:47.223
Victor! Victor! Victor, stop!


00:15:52.104 --> 00:15:53.833
<i>I've got rings on my fingers</i>


00:15:54.006 --> 00:15:55.098
<i>And glitter in my hair</i>


00:15:55.273 --> 00:15:59.369
<i>I've got a one-way ticket
And I just got here</i>


00:15:59.544 --> 00:16:00.875
<i>I'm gonna run...</i>


00:16:01.046 --> 00:16:03.810
- Ha-ha-ha.
- Victor, what are you doing?


00:16:04.249 --> 00:16:05.546
Victor!


00:16:05.717 --> 00:16:08.948
Victor, where did you put my clothes?


00:16:09.121 --> 00:16:11.282
- Surprise!
- What? No.


00:16:14.793 --> 00:16:16.420
I'm gonna kill you. Victor!


00:16:26.338 --> 00:16:27.498
Oh, hi, Katie.


00:16:27.673 --> 00:16:29.072
You are evil. Let me in.


00:16:29.241 --> 00:16:32.677
I control every lock on this property.


00:16:32.844 --> 00:16:34.505
Crap.


00:16:37.916 --> 00:16:39.611
This is insane.


00:16:39.785 --> 00:16:43.846
Yeah, try the shed, it's unlocked, idiot.


00:16:53.632 --> 00:16:55.725
You gotta be kidding me.


00:16:57.469 --> 00:16:59.096
Crap.


00:17:02.407 --> 00:17:06.002
How did such an untalented daughter
spring from my loins?


00:17:06.178 --> 00:17:09.978
Focus, Ms. Gail. We are making
an offering to your personal deity.


00:17:10.148 --> 00:17:12.275
Tell him to give me fame and fortune.


00:17:12.451 --> 00:17:14.146
Not exactly how it works.


00:17:14.319 --> 00:17:16.879
<i>Now, breathe through your Mula Bandha.</i>


00:17:17.055 --> 00:17:20.115
Oh, honey, if I could do that,
I'd get a million hits on YouTube.


00:17:20.292 --> 00:17:22.522
How much longer is this gonna take?
Ugh.


00:17:22.694 --> 00:17:24.821
The prayer or the fame and fortune?


00:17:27.165 --> 00:17:28.632
Ha, ha. See you later.


00:17:34.806 --> 00:17:36.671
Victor.


00:17:40.512 --> 00:17:41.945
Katie?


00:17:43.148 --> 00:17:45.378
- Luke.
- Katie.


00:17:45.584 --> 00:17:48.849
- Are you wearing a doormat?
- Yes.


00:17:49.020 --> 00:17:51.784
- Welcome.
- Why, thank you.


00:17:52.824 --> 00:17:54.655
The truth. Um...


00:17:55.961 --> 00:17:59.294
My stepbrother locked me
outside of the house.


00:17:59.464 --> 00:18:00.795
Naked.


00:18:01.833 --> 00:18:04.131
Oh, sorry. You should...
You should take my jacket.


00:18:04.302 --> 00:18:05.826
Oh.
- Oh, no, no.


00:18:08.273 --> 00:18:09.365
There.


00:18:09.541 --> 00:18:12.738
- Thanks. Now the pants.
- Hmm?


00:18:17.349 --> 00:18:18.976
I'm kidding.


00:18:19.518 --> 00:18:21.349
- You got me.
- Ha, ha.


00:18:21.686 --> 00:18:22.710
No, no.


00:18:22.888 --> 00:18:26.289
One more parent-teacher conference,
I swear I'm gonna lose it.


00:18:26.458 --> 00:18:28.653
Look at me. I'm an educator.


00:18:29.261 --> 00:18:33.925
I have no real skills. And I will die
before I go back to my daddy's farm.


00:18:34.432 --> 00:18:38.232
You tell my personal deity
to help me achieve Guy Morgan. Do it.


00:18:38.403 --> 00:18:40.997
I'll put another banana on the altar.


00:18:44.876 --> 00:18:46.537
What is that?


00:18:47.112 --> 00:18:49.376
Do you hear angels singing?


00:18:49.548 --> 00:18:51.516
Perhaps the gods
have answered your prayer.


00:18:52.717 --> 00:18:54.446
Hey. What...?


00:19:07.299 --> 00:19:09.790
<i>- This is Gail Van Ravensway.
Hello.</i>


00:19:09.968 --> 00:19:11.595
Guy Morgan here. How are you?


00:19:11.770 --> 00:19:13.897
Oh, well, hello, Guy.


00:19:14.072 --> 00:19:16.336
What a surprise
to see you calling this number.


00:19:16.508 --> 00:19:17.532
Do you hear this?


00:19:17.709 --> 00:19:19.370
<i>I can justify</i>


00:19:19.544 --> 00:19:21.239
That's the demo your girl, Katie...


00:19:21.413 --> 00:19:23.745
<i>... slipped into my briefcase.</i>


00:19:23.915 --> 00:19:26.110
And it sounds like money, dear.


00:19:26.284 --> 00:19:28.149
She gave you a CD?


00:19:28.320 --> 00:19:31.687
Oh, well. Well, ain't that the berries.


00:19:32.924 --> 00:19:36.792
Ravi, what frigging god did you pray to?


00:19:38.029 --> 00:19:42.125
Guy, yeah, it seems someone's
not being entirely honest here.


00:19:44.102 --> 00:19:46.297
Katie, somebody get that door!


00:19:47.439 --> 00:19:48.997
So...


00:19:49.875 --> 00:19:52.002
...that meeting today...


00:19:52.177 --> 00:19:54.975
...it was obvious
that your dad doesn't get you.


00:19:55.313 --> 00:19:57.372
He's an idiot for not liking your music.


00:19:57.549 --> 00:19:59.983
Well, it's... It's complicated.


00:20:00.252 --> 00:20:01.446
I'm gonna just, uh...


00:20:02.921 --> 00:20:04.821
Is it as complicated as me...


00:20:04.990 --> 00:20:08.118
...getting stuck outside
in only a welcome mat?


00:20:08.393 --> 00:20:12.124
That's not complicated.
That is a gift from God.


00:20:17.035 --> 00:20:19.833
Luke. Katie. What are you doing?


00:20:20.005 --> 00:20:23.065
Well, it seems your brother
is Satan's very own personal Mini-Me.


00:20:23.241 --> 00:20:25.505
Oh, I know, tell me about it. Come on in.


00:20:29.481 --> 00:20:31.142
Oh, my God, did you work out today?


00:20:32.817 --> 00:20:34.114
- Sit down.
- Ooh, look at this.


00:20:34.286 --> 00:20:37.380
- Ha, ha. Some lemonade.
- Why, thank you.


00:20:37.555 --> 00:20:40.023
You know, my stepsister,
she has body issues...


00:20:40.191 --> 00:20:42.352
...so I don't like
to discourage her nudity.


00:20:42.527 --> 00:20:43.721
That's interesting.


00:20:43.895 --> 00:20:46.659
- She's absolutely lovely...
- Would you like an appetizer?


00:20:46.831 --> 00:20:48.059
<i>Oh, fromage.</i>


00:20:48.233 --> 00:20:49.860
I only have cheese.


00:20:53.038 --> 00:20:55.006
I just got off the phone
with Guy Morgan.


00:20:55.173 --> 00:20:57.073
Your phone.


00:21:00.111 --> 00:21:02.978
He just loved that little demo
you left him.


00:21:03.148 --> 00:21:04.706
I have underestimated you.


00:21:05.283 --> 00:21:07.114
It'd make me proud
if I cared about you.


00:21:07.285 --> 00:21:10.379
- I didn't lie about anything.
- Oh, but, chicken, you did.


00:21:10.555 --> 00:21:13.183
At least that's what Guy thinks,
now that I've clarified.


00:21:13.358 --> 00:21:17.556
I told him it was Bev's demo
and that you stole it from her.


00:21:17.729 --> 00:21:20.994
- But you can't do that. That's my song.
- It's Bev's song.


00:21:21.166 --> 00:21:24.602
And Guy can't wait to see her perform it
at the Showcase.


00:21:24.769 --> 00:21:27.897
If you try to contact him, I'll deny
everything and lock you in the basement.


00:21:28.073 --> 00:21:33.204
- She can't sing to save her life.
- No, but you can, can't you?


00:21:34.479 --> 00:21:36.640
Now, let's hear this amazing voice.


00:21:42.053 --> 00:21:46.683
<i>Like a malignant tumor
She's got no sense of humor</i>


00:21:46.858 --> 00:21:50.954
<i>Just like a swollen blister
It's best to just resist her</i>


00:21:51.129 --> 00:21:54.895
<i>She's not exactly a witch
She's just a terrible bi...</i>


00:21:55.367 --> 00:21:57.028
Well, your lyrics stink.


00:21:57.202 --> 00:21:59.363
But Guy's right, you've got chops.


00:22:02.607 --> 00:22:05.303
Do you know what other instruments
I'm good at?


00:22:05.877 --> 00:22:09.335
I have a feeling I could get in trouble
with a question like that.


00:22:09.781 --> 00:22:11.749
I like trouble.


00:22:13.284 --> 00:22:14.410
Hey, kids.


00:22:15.720 --> 00:22:19.156
- Good evening, Miss Van Ravensway.
- Sorry, I need you to go. Now.


00:22:19.324 --> 00:22:22.088
Family emergency. I need Bev
to help me pass a kidney stone.


00:22:22.260 --> 00:22:26.094
- So she had a lovely evening. Ta-ta.
- Are you trying to ruin my life?


00:22:26.398 --> 00:22:31.631
I have figured out a way for you
to wow Guy Morgan in the Showcase.


00:22:31.836 --> 00:22:34.304
- So you do think I've improved?
- Oh, no, honey.


00:22:34.572 --> 00:22:37.132
But my month of spiritual devotion
has taught me...


00:22:37.308 --> 00:22:39.276
...that God works in annoying ways.


00:22:39.444 --> 00:22:42.504
How am I to wow Guy Morgan
if I supposedly can't sing?


00:22:42.680 --> 00:22:45.740
You can't, but Katie can.


00:22:45.917 --> 00:22:48.613
- What?
- I know. Like I said, annoying.


00:22:48.787 --> 00:22:52.086
We'll record her voice
and you will lip synch.


00:22:52.257 --> 00:22:54.088
What if I don't want to?


00:22:55.193 --> 00:22:58.924
Don't you get snarky with me,
you ungrateful toad.


00:22:59.097 --> 00:23:01.156
- I saved your life.
- You didn't do anything.


00:23:01.332 --> 00:23:03.596
- My dad married you.
- Yeah, and then he died.


00:23:03.768 --> 00:23:07.329
I tried to put you in foster care,
but they was all fulled up on ugly.


00:23:07.505 --> 00:23:08.995
- Funny.
- I thought it was...


00:23:09.174 --> 00:23:10.641
...because you don't wanna look bad.


00:23:12.243 --> 00:23:14.370
Katie, if you don't sing...


00:23:14.546 --> 00:23:17.674
...I'm gonna find a way for that savings
your dad left to disappear.


00:23:18.083 --> 00:23:22.281
That means, you forget college,
moving out, you're stuck here with me.


00:23:22.454 --> 00:23:26.288
But, pumpkin, we're gonna have
so much fun growing old together.


00:23:26.458 --> 00:23:29.359
Why don't you just have her perform
if you like her so much?


00:23:29.527 --> 00:23:31.791
Because, honey, look at you.


00:23:31.963 --> 00:23:34.090
You are a star.


00:23:34.265 --> 00:23:38.463
That is what Guy Morgan needs.
You, the star.


00:23:38.636 --> 00:23:40.194
I'm a star.


00:23:40.371 --> 00:23:44.535
- A bright, gassy star.
- Yes, you are.


00:23:44.709 --> 00:23:47.109
And Guy Morgan is gonna
give you a swimming pool...


00:23:47.278 --> 00:23:49.246
...shaped just like Colin Farrell.


00:23:49.414 --> 00:23:50.972
Every part of him.


00:23:51.149 --> 00:23:54.676
Or, Bev, you could just see every part
of Colin Farrell on the Internet.


00:23:54.853 --> 00:23:57.617
And just leave me out of this.


00:23:58.890 --> 00:24:01.450
- Okay, so how do we do this?
- First rule of Lie Club...


00:24:01.626 --> 00:24:03.526
...is don't talk about Lie Club.


00:24:04.129 --> 00:24:06.029
Which includes you, Katie.


00:24:06.197 --> 00:24:08.893
As far as everyone knows,
you can't sing.


00:24:09.067 --> 00:24:11.126
And no more talking to Luke or Guy.


00:24:11.302 --> 00:24:12.667
Are we clear?


00:24:13.104 --> 00:24:14.298
Crystal.


00:24:16.241 --> 00:24:19.233
Yeah, Dad, we're about to meet
some fresh talent right now.


00:24:19.410 --> 00:24:23.403
Remember when you signed Jay-Z?
No, you passed on him, my bad.


00:24:23.581 --> 00:24:26.049
Um, this is like that,
except it's gonna be brilliant.


00:24:26.217 --> 00:24:27.548
Yeah. Okay.


00:24:27.719 --> 00:24:29.846
- Yeah, okay. Bye.
- Dude, what'd he say?


00:24:30.021 --> 00:24:31.545
These guys you told me about are good?


00:24:31.723 --> 00:24:35.090
Yes. The Oral Majority has potential.
They'll be here any second.


00:24:35.260 --> 00:24:37.956
Talking about potential,
how was your little date with Bev?


00:24:38.129 --> 00:24:40.393
- Her mom kicked me out.
- I told you. Bev is drama.


00:24:40.565 --> 00:24:42.123
Technically, it was Gail's drama.


00:24:42.300 --> 00:24:44.427
But Bev's interesting, man. She's...


00:24:44.602 --> 00:24:46.069
I'm worried she's bonkers.


00:24:46.237 --> 00:24:49.070
See, my last girlfriend, she was hot,
but absolutely mental.


00:24:49.240 --> 00:24:51.902
I need a girl who's not gonna be
shipped to the loony bin.


00:24:52.076 --> 00:24:53.839
Hang on, I'm gonna hit the facilities.


00:24:54.012 --> 00:24:55.707
Facilities. That's a new one.


00:24:56.147 --> 00:24:58.843
- Hey, man. Sorry we're late.
- Hey, what's good, y'all?


00:24:59.017 --> 00:25:01.747
Nobody talks to my boy
until he comes from the facilities.


00:25:01.920 --> 00:25:03.114
We're here to impress.


00:25:03.288 --> 00:25:05.552
- Clear, right?
- Got it.


00:25:09.394 --> 00:25:11.862
<i>When you're fighting just to keep it sane</i>


00:25:12.030 --> 00:25:14.294
<i>Throw your will
At the eye of the hurricane</i>


00:25:14.465 --> 00:25:16.660
<i>- Sing it out
- Eh-oh, eh-oh, eh-oh</i>


00:25:16.834 --> 00:25:20.201
<i>- Help me sing it out
- Eh-oh, eh-oh, eh-oh</i>


00:25:20.371 --> 00:25:22.896
<i>If you wanna find out who you are
Stop running</i>


00:25:23.074 --> 00:25:26.339
<i>In the end you'll figure out
It's all about nothing</i>


00:25:26.511 --> 00:25:31.813
<i>All night, it's gonna be all right
Hey, hey, hey, hey</i>


00:25:31.983 --> 00:25:38.718
<i>All right
Turn your dreams into your life</i>


00:25:39.924 --> 00:25:41.414
That's good.


00:25:48.466 --> 00:25:51.765
I'm clean. No one followed me.
And I got your intel.


00:25:52.604 --> 00:25:54.936
Oh, Katie, baby, your life sucks.


00:25:55.106 --> 00:25:57.006
Trust me, it gets worse.


00:25:58.042 --> 00:26:01.637
Okay, dude, those guys, they
just went Oral Majority on me in there...


00:26:01.813 --> 00:26:04.008
- I was trying to hold them back...
- You're right.


00:26:04.182 --> 00:26:06.116
They have potential and they're great.


00:26:06.284 --> 00:26:11.517
But first, my talent-finding friend,
promise me no more auditions in the bogs.


00:26:11.689 --> 00:26:13.884
- The what?
- The loo.


00:26:14.425 --> 00:26:16.188
- Bathroom. Toilet.
- Got it.


00:26:16.361 --> 00:26:18.955
All right. Okay, come on.
I wanna show you something.


00:26:19.564 --> 00:26:22.863
So now I have to rehearse in secret.


00:26:23.034 --> 00:26:24.501
Why not not rehearse?


00:26:24.669 --> 00:26:26.694
Make Bev sound bad. What do you care?


00:26:26.871 --> 00:26:29.863
No song, no savings account. No life.


00:26:32.043 --> 00:26:34.477
People. Coming. Now.


00:26:38.016 --> 00:26:39.847
Okay.


00:26:40.418 --> 00:26:42.784
Dude, what are we doing?
The suspense is killing me.


00:26:43.121 --> 00:26:44.884
Can you grab the mike?


00:26:45.056 --> 00:26:47.047
Not about to serenade
a brother, are you?


00:26:47.225 --> 00:26:49.056
Dude, with bromance, comes a fine line.


00:26:49.227 --> 00:26:51.525
That I shall not cross.


00:26:51.996 --> 00:26:54.294
So sing something.


00:26:55.967 --> 00:26:57.434
Okay.


00:27:01.572 --> 00:27:04.370
<i>I'm lost in a world
That rattles my brain</i>


00:27:04.542 --> 00:27:07.033
<i>I'm cleaning up my life
From the mess you made</i>


00:27:07.211 --> 00:27:08.610
<i>Oh, oh</i>


00:27:09.080 --> 00:27:11.071
<i>Whoa, oh, oh, oh</i>


00:27:12.884 --> 00:27:15.352
<i>My soul's in debt, but my bills are paid</i>


00:27:15.520 --> 00:27:18.045
<i>I'd give anything just to make an escape</i>


00:27:18.222 --> 00:27:19.814
<i>Oh, oh</i>


00:27:20.325 --> 00:27:21.952
<i>Whoa, oh, oh, oh</i>


00:27:22.960 --> 00:27:25.895
<i>So you can keep
Knocking, knocking, knocking</i>


00:27:26.064 --> 00:27:28.396
<i>Baby, you're rockin'
But there ain't no way I'm ever letting you in</i>


00:27:28.566 --> 00:27:30.033
<i>He's amazing.</i>


00:27:31.436 --> 00:27:33.097
<i>Not again</i>


00:27:34.038 --> 00:27:36.871
<i>So keep on
Knocking, knocking, knocking</i>


00:27:37.041 --> 00:27:42.240
<i>But, baby, you're better off walking
'Cause I ain't gonna let you in</i>


00:27:42.413 --> 00:27:43.971
<i>Never again</i>


00:27:45.083 --> 00:27:47.677
<i>I went out on a limb again</i>


00:27:47.852 --> 00:27:50.412
<i>I guess I had to lose to win</i>


00:27:50.588 --> 00:27:54.957
<i>I was too confused to know
Which way to turn</i>


00:27:56.361 --> 00:27:59.023
<i>- And she could be a millionaire...
- Crap.</i>


00:27:59.197 --> 00:28:01.461
<i>- Gail needs me to drive her home.
- I don't care</i>


00:28:01.632 --> 00:28:04.294
<i>'Cause, baby, there's nobody home</i>


00:28:04.469 --> 00:28:06.960
<i>Nobody's home at all, yeah</i>


00:28:11.442 --> 00:28:13.569
- What? Did you write that?
- Yeah.


00:28:13.745 --> 00:28:16.373
Reminds me of, um... Uh...


00:28:16.547 --> 00:28:19.880
- Danger Fruit, right? Danger Fruit.
- Ha, ha. Because I wrote their album too.


00:28:20.151 --> 00:28:22.642
Shut up. Took me forever
to find that bootleg online.


00:28:22.820 --> 00:28:24.811
- I love that album. That's crazy.
- Yeah.


00:28:24.989 --> 00:28:27.287
My dad doesn't know.
And he thought the record...


00:28:27.458 --> 00:28:29.153
...was a pile of crap.


00:28:29.427 --> 00:28:31.122
He thinks writing's a waste of time.


00:28:31.562 --> 00:28:35.396
Because he basically wants me
to be like him. Only with better hair.


00:28:35.867 --> 00:28:39.963
But the first thing I thought when
I heard those guys in the urinals was...


00:28:40.138 --> 00:28:41.162
...good acoustics.


00:28:41.572 --> 00:28:45.406
Second thought was these guys,
these guys could be great.


00:28:45.576 --> 00:28:47.168
If you gave them your song.


00:28:48.579 --> 00:28:50.240
Mate, that's a brilliant idea.


00:28:50.982 --> 00:28:53.678
- So put them in the Showcase?
- Put them in the Showcase.


00:28:53.851 --> 00:28:55.182
Yeah.


00:28:56.854 --> 00:29:03.384
<i>You can never tell where this might go</i>


00:29:03.694 --> 00:29:04.991
You wrote that song today?


00:29:05.163 --> 00:29:08.621
- You've been home for what, two hours?
- It's like an answer to his song.


00:29:08.900 --> 00:29:10.197
You really like this guy.


00:29:10.368 --> 00:29:12.063
Yeah, I'm an idiot.


00:29:12.236 --> 00:29:14.431
You have to sing that for him.


00:29:14.605 --> 00:29:18.097
What if you sang to him in secret?


00:29:19.911 --> 00:29:22.709
At the dance. Ta-da.


00:29:26.317 --> 00:29:29.150
Okay, I know the card's
like, really cheesy, but...


00:29:31.189 --> 00:29:33.657
Oh, God, I hope you like it.


00:29:33.991 --> 00:29:37.483
Ange, it's beautiful,
but are you crazy?


00:29:37.662 --> 00:29:39.687
No, I know you're crazy.


00:29:39.864 --> 00:29:40.888
Am not.


00:29:41.933 --> 00:29:44.925
- What if he doesn't even like me?
- You'll both be in disguise.


00:29:45.102 --> 00:29:47.798
It's your chance to see
if he was really flirting with you.


00:29:47.972 --> 00:29:50.532
I was naked. Of course he was flirting.


00:29:50.708 --> 00:29:53.404
And why even torture myself?
It's not like I can have him.


00:29:53.578 --> 00:29:55.512
Why not? Tell him how you feel.


00:29:55.680 --> 00:29:59.707
If he feels the same way, you can reveal
your hot self and he won't tell Gail.


00:30:00.084 --> 00:30:03.178
And if he hates the song,
leave the disguise on.


00:30:06.123 --> 00:30:07.647
Okay.


00:30:07.959 --> 00:30:09.551
I'm going to the dance.


00:30:09.727 --> 00:30:11.058
That's my girl.


00:30:11.329 --> 00:30:15.322
<i>Maurice, no, no.
Again, in Français, longer legs.</i>


00:30:15.500 --> 00:30:18.799
I wouldn't go in your closet
for a little while if I were you.


00:30:18.970 --> 00:30:20.733
What? Why?


00:30:20.905 --> 00:30:22.270
Hey. Wake up.


00:30:26.177 --> 00:30:27.735
Katie!


00:30:27.912 --> 00:30:31.348
The cat has pooped in my closet.
I need you to clean it up.


00:30:31.516 --> 00:30:33.006
Go.


00:30:33.184 --> 00:30:34.913
I told you we don't have a cat.


00:30:35.086 --> 00:30:36.417
Angie, heads up.


00:30:38.389 --> 00:30:39.686
Katie!


00:30:44.896 --> 00:30:46.625
What's going on?


00:30:46.797 --> 00:30:48.230
Nothing.


00:30:48.399 --> 00:30:51.527
I am, uh, re-organizing and labeling. I...


00:30:51.702 --> 00:30:54.000
I took up crochet.
Do you want new socks?


00:30:54.171 --> 00:30:58.232
I would make you a sweater, but I hear
that the arms, that they're really hard.


00:31:01.479 --> 00:31:05.643
Oh, you thought you could sneak off
and go to the dance.


00:31:05.816 --> 00:31:08.046
After what you pulled today with Guy.


00:31:08.219 --> 00:31:09.652
Oh, no, no.


00:31:09.820 --> 00:31:12.311
Oh, no, no, no.


00:31:12.490 --> 00:31:14.788
You're on Victor watch tonight...


00:31:14.959 --> 00:31:17.655
...tomorrow night and every night.


00:31:17.828 --> 00:31:18.852
Fun.


00:31:19.030 --> 00:31:22.158
I'll give Victor all the mothering
you don't have time for.


00:31:22.333 --> 00:31:25.734
Oh, I wish you could be my mommy.


00:31:26.604 --> 00:31:28.629
I'm off to my cinnamon colonic.


00:31:32.610 --> 00:31:34.976
Hey. Get down.
You're gonna break yourself.


00:31:35.313 --> 00:31:37.577
Or worse, the furniture.


00:31:37.882 --> 00:31:40.976
Hello?
- Hey.


00:31:41.252 --> 00:31:44.415
- You look like you're having fun.
- Always.


00:31:44.755 --> 00:31:47.815
Well, I couldn't let you not go to the dance
without me.


00:31:47.992 --> 00:31:50.392
Besides, we have six hours
of shirtless Team Jacob.


00:31:50.561 --> 00:31:53.496
So let's just get this party started.


00:31:53.664 --> 00:31:57.691
- So is Victor driving you nuts?
- I swear to you, he's not human.


00:31:57.969 --> 00:32:01.268
I mean, can you really blame him, though?
Just look at this family.


00:32:02.473 --> 00:32:03.770
Victor, what are you doing?


00:32:13.751 --> 00:32:16.015
Oh, no. Great.


00:32:16.187 --> 00:32:18.382
Eh, she actually looks prettier
that way.


00:32:18.990 --> 00:32:22.016
True. Ugh. Whatever.


00:32:23.194 --> 00:32:26.322
Why did I ever think that tonight
could've been something special.


00:32:27.098 --> 00:32:29.362
Think Bev's all over Luke at the dance
right now?


00:32:29.533 --> 00:32:31.831
They're probably making out. See?


00:32:32.003 --> 00:32:35.200
- Victor, give it a rest.
- Just check it out. Come on.


00:32:38.409 --> 00:32:41.037
<i>Luke is gonna produce
whoever wins the Showcase.</i>


00:32:41.212 --> 00:32:44.272
<i>So we need a little insurance.</i>


00:32:44.448 --> 00:32:47.645
<i>- I know what I'm doing, Mother.
Do you?</i>


00:32:48.552 --> 00:32:51.419
I can't take it anymore, okay?


00:32:51.589 --> 00:32:53.648
I'm taking my life into my own hands.


00:32:53.824 --> 00:32:54.916
I'm talking to Luke.


00:32:55.526 --> 00:32:58.017
- Finally.
- Okay, but we have gotta be home...


00:32:58.195 --> 00:32:59.662
...before Gail gets here.


00:33:00.398 --> 00:33:01.729
What about the demon spawn?


00:33:01.899 --> 00:33:02.923
Mm-hm.


00:33:03.100 --> 00:33:04.499
Right.


00:33:05.503 --> 00:33:06.902
Okay, just watch him.


00:33:09.974 --> 00:33:11.236
Hmm.


00:33:16.047 --> 00:33:18.038
Is that all you've got, Angela?


00:33:18.716 --> 00:33:19.740
Ravi?


00:33:21.419 --> 00:33:23.944
My sister could catch that, jerknut.


00:33:24.121 --> 00:33:26.555
Put some nuts in that sack, ref.


00:33:28.693 --> 00:33:31.253
Miss Katie, I am most startled.


00:33:31.429 --> 00:33:32.623
Obviously.


00:33:33.164 --> 00:33:35.655
All right. All right. Don't hate me.


00:33:35.833 --> 00:33:37.391
Okay, don't hate me. I'm sorry.


00:33:37.568 --> 00:33:40.935
But my name ain't Ravi. It's Tony.


00:33:41.472 --> 00:33:44.600
- Tony.
- Tony Gupta from Jersey.


00:33:44.775 --> 00:33:47.437
- From Jersey.
- I am half Indian.


00:33:47.812 --> 00:33:51.213
My friends call me Meatball
because I'm half Italian.


00:33:51.382 --> 00:33:53.247
Truth is I always wanted to be an actor.


00:33:53.617 --> 00:33:55.141
But I never got my shot.


00:33:55.319 --> 00:33:57.549
I'm working at KFC,
and one day, Gail comes in...


00:33:57.722 --> 00:34:00.122
...she's like, "Are you Indian?"
I'm like, "What?"


00:34:00.291 --> 00:34:02.486
She's like, "Are you a guru?"
I'm like:


00:34:02.660 --> 00:34:04.150
"Who is asking?"


00:34:04.428 --> 00:34:07.795
She says, "Someone
who's paying for some spiritual guidance."


00:34:07.965 --> 00:34:10.559
And I'm like, "Whaa! It's a miracle!"


00:34:10.735 --> 00:34:15.104
I finally get a chance to do
a total immersion into a character.


00:34:15.406 --> 00:34:17.670
Real training and I get paid.
Are you kidding me?


00:34:17.842 --> 00:34:20.242
Ravi is my King Lear.


00:34:20.578 --> 00:34:23.206
<i>You wanna hear
the monologue from My Fair Lady?</i>


00:34:23.380 --> 00:34:24.574
- Oy, mate.
- No, thanks.


00:34:25.783 --> 00:34:28.479
I'm sorry I barged in. Whoops.


00:34:31.288 --> 00:34:34.951
Your secret's safe with me, okay?
But I need to ask you a favor.


00:34:35.626 --> 00:34:37.685
- Meatball.
- Ha, Meatball.


00:34:37.862 --> 00:34:40.330
Please watch Victor tonight
so I can go to the dance?


00:34:40.498 --> 00:34:41.556
Are you kidding me? Done.


00:34:43.134 --> 00:34:44.465
Blow it up.


00:34:46.403 --> 00:34:47.961
Thank you.


00:34:57.782 --> 00:34:59.181
Whoa.


00:34:59.350 --> 00:35:01.978
How am I supposed to find Luke
if everybody's got a mask?


00:35:02.153 --> 00:35:05.213
I never said this was
gonna be easy. Let's do some recon.


00:35:06.590 --> 00:35:08.922
I am Assistant Principal
Dorothy Plumberg.


00:35:09.093 --> 00:35:12.324
No drinking. No texting. No kissing.


00:35:15.032 --> 00:35:18.001
Luke? No. Luke Morgan?


00:35:18.169 --> 00:35:21.798
No leaving the premises
and no experiencing joy of any kind.


00:35:22.506 --> 00:35:24.838
Luke? Ugh.


00:35:30.214 --> 00:35:31.647
Where is he?


00:35:32.483 --> 00:35:35.281
That reminds me.
I got a new act for you to listen to.


00:35:35.452 --> 00:35:37.113
- Now?
- No time like it.


00:35:37.288 --> 00:35:39.722
- Dude, not again...
- We're called Big Pain Ticket.


00:35:43.227 --> 00:35:46.788
<i>I wanna kiss your apocalypse</i>


00:35:46.964 --> 00:35:50.297
<i>Wrap you in my Armageddon</i>


00:35:50.467 --> 00:35:52.662
<i>Sing you a twisted serenade</i>


00:35:52.870 --> 00:35:55.600
They're good, but I'm worried
that chain saw's unsafe.


00:35:55.773 --> 00:35:58.207
Dude, the chain saw's,
like, the best part.


00:36:05.015 --> 00:36:06.073
I think I found him.


00:36:06.250 --> 00:36:08.514
Well, he is blond.


00:36:11.622 --> 00:36:13.920
Oh, my God, what is she doing here?


00:36:15.826 --> 00:36:18.124
I hate teenage desperation.


00:36:18.295 --> 00:36:19.694
What are you doing here?


00:36:19.864 --> 00:36:22.697
Oh, honey, the prize pig
doesn't win the blue ribbon...


00:36:22.867 --> 00:36:24.892
...by covering up its third best asset.


00:36:25.069 --> 00:36:28.004
A, what does that even mean
and, B, did you just call me a pig?


00:36:28.172 --> 00:36:30.003
Honey, I saw you making sweet love...


00:36:30.174 --> 00:36:32.642
...to a plate of Swedish meatballs
at the snack table.


00:36:35.079 --> 00:36:37.206
It's now or never, babe.


00:36:38.749 --> 00:36:42.185
- What if she recognizes me?
- I'll distract her. Go.


00:36:42.353 --> 00:36:44.548
- So was I right or was I right?
- You were right.


00:36:44.722 --> 00:36:47.589
You have very cool taste.
Any more auditions in the men's...


00:36:47.758 --> 00:36:49.692
...and you're fired.


00:36:52.730 --> 00:36:56.257
- I know your secret.
- Which secret is that?


00:36:58.869 --> 00:37:00.359
I heard you sing at school.


00:37:00.604 --> 00:37:01.730
You were amazing.


00:37:01.906 --> 00:37:02.964
Do I know you?


00:37:07.311 --> 00:37:09.905
- I wanna show you something.
- What's your name?


00:37:12.249 --> 00:37:14.308
Angela, what are you doing?


00:37:14.952 --> 00:37:17.443
I'd like to make a request.


00:37:21.959 --> 00:37:24.792
I will make your night. I promise.


00:37:24.962 --> 00:37:26.327
Miss Van R.


00:37:26.964 --> 00:37:29.364
Is it true you wanted to be a dancer
when you were younger...


00:37:29.533 --> 00:37:30.727
...but were never good enough?


00:37:32.102 --> 00:37:33.763
Who told you that?


00:37:51.488 --> 00:37:52.921
Well, now, how lovely.


00:37:53.090 --> 00:37:56.287
But I've seen better dancing
in a Filipino prison, sugar.


00:37:56.460 --> 00:37:57.586
Oh!


00:37:57.761 --> 00:38:01.993
Really? Because I think
I just challenged you to a dance battle.


00:38:06.337 --> 00:38:09.431
Would Luke Morgan please pick up
the white courtesy phone?


00:38:09.606 --> 00:38:12.507
Luke Morgan, white courtesy phone.


00:38:17.281 --> 00:38:20.011
Hold on. What is that?
You've never seen a guitar before?


00:38:20.351 --> 00:38:23.047
You hid a guitar in there.
You hiding anything else?


00:38:23.220 --> 00:38:24.482
Follow me.


00:38:29.526 --> 00:38:31.357
Oh, wow.


00:38:33.831 --> 00:38:39.394
Madam, while your exquisite eyes
tell of a radiant, but mischievous beauty...


00:38:40.270 --> 00:38:42.170
...I have grown impatient.


00:38:42.339 --> 00:38:46.036
Off with your veil,
so that I may know the truth.


00:38:47.544 --> 00:38:48.738
Or not.


00:38:51.015 --> 00:38:54.041
I'm hoping this answers
a lot of your questions.


00:39:00.257 --> 00:39:03.818
<i>I can see it from the spark in your eyes</i>


00:39:05.129 --> 00:39:09.361
<i>You believe in all the things
You've denied</i>


00:39:09.533 --> 00:39:13.060
<i>You wanna fly
And leave your worries behind</i>


00:39:13.237 --> 00:39:17.230
<i>Don't you? Don't you?</i>


00:39:19.209 --> 00:39:22.542
<i>Well, now I'm knocking
At your front door</i>


00:39:24.314 --> 00:39:28.011
<i>And I'm looking for the right cure</i>


00:39:28.685 --> 00:39:32.382
<i>I'm still a little bit unsure</i>


00:39:32.856 --> 00:39:35.689
Okay, now take off that veil.


00:39:36.160 --> 00:39:37.252
Uh-uh.


00:42:16.186 --> 00:42:18.780
I think I've blown something.


00:42:18.956 --> 00:42:22.016
Does anyone else smell cinnamon?


00:42:24.628 --> 00:42:26.186
Move it, fatso.


00:42:27.931 --> 00:42:34.530
<i>You can never tell where this might go</i>


00:42:35.272 --> 00:42:38.901
Okay, you are blowing my mind.
You have to show me who you are.


00:42:51.455 --> 00:42:52.888
- We have to go.
- What?


00:42:53.056 --> 00:42:55.081
- Come.
- No, Ange.


00:42:55.259 --> 00:42:57.819
In the middle of a really big moment
right now.


00:42:57.995 --> 00:42:59.963
Someone had an accident
and went home.


00:43:02.432 --> 00:43:03.797
I'm so sorry.


00:43:04.501 --> 00:43:05.729
What...? You...?


00:43:06.436 --> 00:43:08.097
Hey. Wait.


00:43:08.272 --> 00:43:09.500
But who are you?


00:43:09.673 --> 00:43:12.267
Over here. Go, go, go.


00:43:20.417 --> 00:43:23.443
- We beat her.
- I love you for this.


00:43:41.905 --> 00:43:43.930
Interesting babysitting attire.


00:43:44.708 --> 00:43:47.643
I should've known
you'd go behind my back again.


00:43:48.078 --> 00:43:51.013
And that Paula Abdul wannabe,
trying to distract me.


00:43:51.348 --> 00:43:53.543
Don't talk about her like that.


00:43:55.552 --> 00:43:58.715
Your friend wants to be a choreographer,
if memory serves.


00:43:58.889 --> 00:44:02.450
She might've made a decent one
if she hadn't gotten herself expelled.


00:44:02.626 --> 00:44:04.890
Guess she can kiss
them Juilliard dreams goodbye.


00:44:05.062 --> 00:44:08.122
Look, I'll do whatever you want.
Okay? Just leave Ange out of this.


00:44:08.432 --> 00:44:11.560
That depends if you pull another stunt
like tonight, sugar.


00:44:12.469 --> 00:44:15.597
- I won't.
- I'll be taking this.


00:44:22.112 --> 00:44:25.343
Only her eyes were piercing out
through this veil, but her voice...


00:44:25.515 --> 00:44:27.574
How hot was the girl
on a scale of one to 10?


00:44:27.751 --> 00:44:29.685
- An 11.
- The hotness scale only goes 10.


00:44:29.853 --> 00:44:31.548
Yeah, this girl has love potential.


00:44:31.722 --> 00:44:34.020
- Ooh, love.
- Shut it.


00:44:35.392 --> 00:44:39.522
We are gonna do this for hours
until we get it right. Even if it takes hours.


00:44:40.497 --> 00:44:44.092
Now, sing like your life depends on it.
Because, sugar, it does.


00:44:45.168 --> 00:44:46.795
We're recording.


00:44:47.104 --> 00:44:48.935
<i>Plug in the mike</i>


00:44:49.106 --> 00:44:50.334
<i>Open the curtain</i>


00:44:50.941 --> 00:44:52.875
<i>Turn on the lights</i>


00:44:53.043 --> 00:44:54.772
<i>I'm through rehearsing</i>


00:44:54.945 --> 00:44:57.277
- Dang, she's good, man.
- Told you, man.


00:44:57.447 --> 00:44:58.675
Check this out, all right?


00:44:58.849 --> 00:45:02.444
Thirty-nine girls in the singing program
which means 85 percent...


00:45:02.619 --> 00:45:04.450
...have music during the sixth period.


00:45:04.621 --> 00:45:06.452
So your girl's in one of those rooms.


00:45:06.656 --> 00:45:08.681
<i>The feeling ignites</i>


00:45:08.859 --> 00:45:10.019
<i>I'm in control</i>


00:45:10.193 --> 00:45:12.161
Oh, cut. Cut.


00:45:12.329 --> 00:45:14.194
That was subpar at best.


00:45:14.364 --> 00:45:16.889
From the top, pretty please.


00:45:17.634 --> 00:45:20.933
<i>Amazing grace</i>


00:45:21.104 --> 00:45:22.662
It's cool, I got this.


00:45:22.839 --> 00:45:25.205
Ladies, all my single ladies.


00:45:25.375 --> 00:45:28.401
My boy Luke here has a special favor
to ask of you, all right?


00:45:28.578 --> 00:45:31.672
He needs vocals
for this big show coming up, so...


00:45:31.848 --> 00:45:33.406
- My name is...
- Luke Morgan.


00:45:33.850 --> 00:45:36.717
You will put me in the Showcase.
Oh, yes, you will.


00:45:37.254 --> 00:45:40.815
- Maybe I could ask you to sing first?
- I am so gonna rock your world.


00:45:41.091 --> 00:45:44.424
<i>I love the way you love me, Luke</i>


00:45:44.594 --> 00:45:47.188
<i>Inside my head every night</i>


00:45:47.364 --> 00:45:49.832
<i>You come and kiss me good night</i>


00:45:50.000 --> 00:45:53.094
<i>Whatever you see is what you get</i>


00:45:53.270 --> 00:45:55.795
Why don't you not suck
and do it again, okay?


00:45:57.541 --> 00:46:02.137
<i>I wanna be with you forever...</i>


00:46:02.312 --> 00:46:05.281
What is going on in here? Disgusting.


00:46:05.449 --> 00:46:08.282
You two boys are not in my class.
Stop. Wait.


00:46:14.324 --> 00:46:17.521
Stop. Wait. Stop.


00:46:36.646 --> 00:46:38.944
<i>I got nothing to lose</i>


00:46:39.115 --> 00:46:40.309
<i>I've been exposed</i>


00:46:40.484 --> 00:46:42.782
<i>I'm paying my dues</i>


00:46:42.953 --> 00:46:44.318
<i>Playing the role</i>


00:46:45.155 --> 00:46:47.282
- Oh, really?
- We are back where we started.


00:46:47.457 --> 00:46:48.583
This is not good.


00:46:50.160 --> 00:46:51.957
That's her. That's her voice.


00:46:52.128 --> 00:46:53.959
Don't think you can get away from me.


00:46:54.130 --> 00:46:56.530
- Step aside. Step aside.
- Please. Wait.


00:46:56.700 --> 00:47:00.136
Okay. But first, why don't you
just both audition for me.


00:47:00.303 --> 00:47:01.327
Listen...


00:47:01.505 --> 00:47:04.941
<i>Luke, you are the one for me, yes you are</i>


00:47:05.108 --> 00:47:06.769
<i>You just don't know it yet</i>


00:47:18.622 --> 00:47:22.615
<i>Make you believe in me</i>


00:47:22.792 --> 00:47:25.784
<i>I can be what you want me to be</i>


00:47:25.962 --> 00:47:29.591
<i>Tonight is the night
Where I make you see</i>


00:47:29.766 --> 00:47:33.702
<i>That I can be
Anything, anything, anything</i>


00:47:33.870 --> 00:47:37.670
<i>I'll make you believe in me</i>


00:47:38.208 --> 00:47:41.109
<i>I can be what you want me to be</i>


00:47:41.278 --> 00:47:44.338
<i>Tonight is the night
Where I make you see</i>


00:47:46.149 --> 00:47:48.083
It was you?


00:47:48.752 --> 00:47:51.846
- Oh, sorry to interrupt.
- Oh, no, honey. Interrupt away.


00:47:52.789 --> 00:47:56.623
I didn't think I'd see you. It was killing me.
Because I felt like we connected.


00:47:58.261 --> 00:48:01.287
Excuse me.
Uh, how exactly did you two connect?


00:48:01.464 --> 00:48:04.228
Yeah, how did we? I mean, we did.


00:48:04.401 --> 00:48:06.528
- Through...
- With your lyrics. They just...


00:48:07.170 --> 00:48:09.900
- I can't get them out of my head.
- My lyrics. Yeah.


00:48:10.173 --> 00:48:11.936
Well, how wonderful.


00:48:12.108 --> 00:48:15.475
But, uh, Bev has to prepare
for her Showcase audition.


00:48:15.645 --> 00:48:17.909
Oh, no. She doesn't need to audition.
You're in.


00:48:19.416 --> 00:48:21.213
Do you wanna grab a bite later?


00:48:21.384 --> 00:48:22.476
- Yeah.
Wait.


00:48:23.420 --> 00:48:24.887
You have a date with detention.


00:48:25.055 --> 00:48:26.522
Actually, he has a date with me.


00:48:26.690 --> 00:48:28.419
Dear me, did I not fire you?


00:48:28.592 --> 00:48:31.288
- I have tenure.
- One call and you're wearing a paper hat...


00:48:31.461 --> 00:48:34.589
...that says "Welcome to McDonald's.
How may I take your order?"


00:48:34.764 --> 00:48:36.254
- Five calls.
- Two calls and text.


00:48:36.433 --> 00:48:38.333
Two calls, a text, several long e-mails.


00:48:38.501 --> 00:48:41.299
One text and a Tweet.
- One text and a re-Tweet.


00:48:41.471 --> 00:48:43.837
Oh, for God's sakes,
go lick a chalkboard.


00:48:44.007 --> 00:48:45.474
Fine.


00:48:46.276 --> 00:48:47.800
I hate you.


00:48:51.448 --> 00:48:55.578
Okay. Um, I'd love to write a song with you.
Let's talk about it tonight?


00:48:55.852 --> 00:48:57.786
- I'd love to.
- Okay, you're on.


00:49:04.361 --> 00:49:05.988
I've always wanted to write a song.


00:49:06.162 --> 00:49:09.359
Maybe I'll write about my skin.
They say love tightens your pores.


00:49:09.532 --> 00:49:10.999
What rhymes with pores?


00:49:11.167 --> 00:49:13.965
Chores. Bores. Sores.


00:49:14.137 --> 00:49:16.332
Katie, I've got a new task for you.


